From 355dd22d6a3190a22eea9764a60ac3e756959bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yp <yp@e5debian>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:08:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/adreno/a6xx: force cold boot on hang recovery

On the recovery path the CX power domain has been cycled, which can
clear the CM3's TCM even though the TCM-retention flag still reads
"retained". Taking the warm-boot path in that case skips the firmware
reload, so the CM3 boots from dead memory and never acks the host OOB
handshake, leaving the GPU stuck in a hang -> recover -> hang loop.

Force a cold boot (full firmware reload and re-init) whenever we are
recovering from a hang.

Origin: liuqin kernel commit 355dd22d6a31 (not upstream). Ported to this
tree as it is; the only difference to the original is where the lines
land, after the a8xx branch that 7.2 has in the cold-or-warm decision.
a6xx_gpu->hung is set at the start of a6xx_recover() and cleared at its
end, after the resume, so it is true on every resume that recovers.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 4808604..45273d3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1376,6 +1376,18 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 		status = GMU_COLD_BOOT;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * On the recovery path the CX power domain has been cycled, which can
+	 * clear the CM3's TCM even though the TCM-retention flag read above
+	 * still reports "retained". Taking the warm-boot path in that case
+	 * skips the firmware reload, so the CM3 boots from dead memory and
+	 * never acks the host OOB handshake, leaving the GPU stuck in a
+	 * hang -> recover -> hang loop. Force a cold boot (full firmware
+	 * reload and re-init) whenever we are recovering from a hang.
+	 */
+	if (a6xx_gpu->hung)
+		status = GMU_COLD_BOOT;
+
 	ret = a6xx_gmu_fw_start(gmu, status);
 	if (ret)
 		goto disable_irq;
-- 
2.54.0

